  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse d&#x2019;urgence pour r&#xe9;duire la morbidit&#xe9; et mortalit&#xe9; li&#xe9;es aux &#xe9;pid&#xe9;mies de chol&#xe9;ra dans 4 provinces hots spots en RDC.
(Sankuru, Sud-Kivu, Tanganyika, Haut-Lomami)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide health assistance to vulnerable communities affected by Cholera in the Democratic Republic of Congo. This WHO project enhances early detection and diagnosis of Cholera cases, provides emergency health kits, deploys epidemiologists, supports disinfection of households and communal spaces, trains health workers, and provides WASH items, among other activities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 127,952 people, including 27,081 women, 74,852 children, and 19,195 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
